Q: Trying unsuccessfully to build a demo JavaFX app native with Liberica NIK A: <p><em><strong>Preface:</strong> Just want to preface this answer with the infamous &quot;works on my machine&quot;. I tested
the following example on Windows 10 and Ubuntu 24.04 WSL 2 and it worked (I needed to pass
<code>-Dprism.forceGPU=true</code> on Linux, but I think that's a WSL-specific issue). I did not test on
other machines.</em></p>
<hr />
<h1>Building GraalVM Native Images via Maven</h1>
<p>There are two ways I can think of to build GraalVM native images via Maven.</p>
<ol>
<li>Use the <code>org.codehaus.mojo:exec-maven-plugin</code> to manually execute the <code>native-image</code> tool.</li>
<li>Use the <code>org.graalvm.buildtools:native-maven-plugin</code>.</li>
</ol>
<p>The <code>native-maven-plugin</code> is the more feature-rich approach. But note <a href="https://github.com/graalvm/native-build-tools/issues/611" rel="nofollow noreferrer">it does not appear to support
toolchains</a>. It requires a GraalVM installation to be specified either via a <code>JAVA_HOME</code> or
<code>GRAALVM_HOME</code> environment variable. Though I'm not sure which takes precedence. Nor am I sure if
<code>JAVA_HOME</code> must be specified if a GraalVM installation is being used to execute Maven itself.</p>
<h2>Example with BellSoft Liberica Full NIK 25</h2>
<p>Here's an example Maven project that can build a native image of a JavaFX application. It assumes
that <em>BellSoft Liberica Full NIK 25+</em> is being used. Where &quot;Full&quot; means the distribution includes
JavaFX and &quot;NIK&quot; (Native Image Kit) means the distribution includes GraalVM tools.</p>
<p>The JavaFX application simply displays the application's module, the environment variables, the
system properties, and the set of modules in the application.</p>
<p>The Maven POM is implemented to be able to demonstrate using the <code>exec-maven-plugin</code> plugin or the
<code>native-maven-plugin</code> plugin. It also allows optionally using toolchains. Additionally, there is
a goal for executing the Java code and a goal for executing the native image. Because of this, the
POM is more complicated than it otherwise could be. You can simplify the POM in your own project.</p>
<p><strong>I did not set up the project to run the tracing agent before building the native image.</strong> You
should probably do that for a real project.</p>
<p>The native image will be located at <code>target/bin/jfxapp[.exe]</code>.</p>
<h3>Profiles</h3>
<p>The POM declares multiple profiles to handle different scenarios.</p>
<div class="s-table-container"><table class="s-table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Profile ID</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>win</code></td>
<td>Appends <code>.cmd</code> to the <code>native-image</code> tool name.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>exec</code></td>
<td>Configures the build to use the <code>exec-maven-plugin</code> plugin to compile the native image.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>buildtools</code></td>
<td>Configures the build to use the <code>native-maven-plugin</code> plugin to compile the native image.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>toolchain</code></td>
<td>Configures the build to use toolchains.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>The <code>win</code> profile is automatically activated when on Windows. The other profiles must be manually
activated.</p>
<p>When the <code>toolchain</code> profile is activated, the toolchain configuration is:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;jdk&gt;
  &lt;version&gt;[25,)&lt;/version&gt;
  &lt;vendor&gt;BellSoft&lt;/vendor&gt;
  &lt;!-- 
    The 'nik' is to distinguish between &quot;normal&quot; and NIK distributions. The
    'full' is to distinguish between &quot;standard&quot; (no JavaFX) and &quot;full&quot; (with
    JavaFX) distributions.

    Edit or remove this, or edit your 'toolchains.xml', as needed so the
    toolchains match.
  --&gt;
  &lt;variant&gt;nik-full&lt;/variant&gt;
&lt;/jdk&gt;
</code></pre>
<h3>Source Code</h3>
<p>Here is the source code of the example.</p>
<h4>Java</h4>
<p>module-info.java:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>module jfxapp {
  requires transitive javafx.graphics;
  requires javafx.controls;

  exports com.example.jfxapp to
      javafx.graphics;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Main.java:</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>package com.example.jfxapp;

import java.io.File;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Locale;
import java.util.Set;
import javafx.application.Application;
import javafx.beans.property.SimpleObjectProperty;
import javafx.beans.value.ObservableValue;
import javafx.geometry.Insets;
import javafx.geometry.Pos;
import javafx.scene.Scene;
import javafx.scene.control.Label;
import javafx.scene.control.ListCell;
import javafx.scene.control.ListView;
import javafx.scene.control.Tab;
import javafx.scene.control.TabPane;
import javafx.scene.control.TableColumn;
import javafx.scene.control.TableView;
import javafx.scene.layout.HBox;
import javafx.scene.layout.Priority;
import javafx.scene.layout.VBox;
import javafx.scene.text.Font;
import javafx.scene.text.FontWeight;
import javafx.stage.Stage;
import javafx.util.Callback;

public class Main extends Application {

  static {
    IO.println(&quot;Main class initialized.&quot;);
  }

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    IO.println(&quot;Launching application.&quot;);
    launch(Main.class, args);
  }

  public Main() {
    IO.println(&quot;Main instance created.&quot;);
  }

  @Override
  public void init() {
    IO.println(&quot;Initializing application.&quot;);
  }

  @Override
  public void start(Stage primaryStage) {
    IO.println(&quot;Starting application.&quot;);

    var appModuleView = createAppModuleView();

    var tabPane = new TabPane();
    tabPane.setTabClosingPolicy(TabPane.TabClosingPolicy.UNAVAILABLE);
    tabPane
        .getTabs()
        .addAll(
            new Tab(&quot;Environment&quot;, createEnvironmentTableView()),
            new Tab(&quot;System Properties&quot;, createSystemPropertyTableView()),
            new Tab(&quot;Modules&quot;, createModuleListView()));
    tabPane.getStyleClass().add(TabPane.STYLE_CLASS_FLOATING);

    var root = new VBox(appModuleView, tabPane);
    VBox.setMargin(appModuleView, new Insets(5));
    VBox.setVgrow(tabPane, Priority.ALWAYS);

    primaryStage.setScene(new Scene(root, 1280, 720));
    primaryStage.setTitle(&quot;JavaFX Application&quot;);
    primaryStage.show();
  }

  @Override
  public void stop() {
    IO.println(&quot;Stopping application.&quot;);
  }

  private HBox createAppModuleView() {
    var label = new Label(&quot;Application Module:&quot;);
    label.setFont(Font.font(&quot;System&quot;, FontWeight.BOLD, -1.0));

    var value = new Label(Main.class.getModule().toString());

    var hbox = new HBox(5, label, value);
    hbox.setAlignment(Pos.CENTER_LEFT);
    return hbox;
  }

  private TableView&lt;Property&gt; createEnvironmentTableView() {
    return createPropertyTable(Property.ofEnvironment());
  }

  private TableView&lt;Property&gt; createSystemPropertyTableView() {
    return createPropertyTable(Property.ofSystemProperties());
  }

  private TableView&lt;Property&gt; createPropertyTable(List&lt;Property&gt; properties) {
    var table = new TableView&lt;Property&gt;();
    table.setColumnResizePolicy(TableView.CONSTRAINED_RESIZE_POLICY_FLEX_LAST_COLUMN);
    table.getItems().addAll(properties);
    table.getItems().sort(Comparator.comparing(Property::key));

    var keyCol = new TableColumn&lt;Property, String&gt;(&quot;Key&quot;);
    keyCol.setCellValueFactory(cellValueFactory(Property::key));
    table.getColumns().add(keyCol);

    var valCol = new TableColumn&lt;Property, String&gt;(&quot;Value&quot;);
    valCol.setCellValueFactory(cellValueFactory(Property::value));
    table.getColumns().add(valCol);

    return table;
  }

  private static &lt;S, T&gt;
      Callback&lt;TableColumn.CellDataFeatures&lt;S, T&gt;, ObservableValue&lt;T&gt;&gt; cellValueFactory(
          Callback&lt;S, T&gt; valueExtractor) {
    return cdf -&gt; new SimpleObjectProperty&lt;&gt;(valueExtractor.call(cdf.getValue()));
  }

  private ListView&lt;Module&gt; createModuleListView() {
    var list = new ListView&lt;Module&gt;();
    list.setCellFactory(_ -&gt; new ListCell&lt;&gt;() {
      @Override
      protected void updateItem(Module item, boolean empty) {
        super.updateItem(item, empty);
        if (empty || item == null) setText(null);
        else setText(item.getName());
      }
    });

    var module = Main.class.getModule();
    var layer = module.isNamed() ? module.getLayer() : ModuleLayer.boot();
    list.getItems().addAll(getAllModules(layer));
    list.getItems().sort(Comparator.comparing(Module::getName));

    return list;
  }

  private static Set&lt;Module&gt; getAllModules(ModuleLayer layer) {
    var modules = new HashSet&lt;Module&gt;();
    modules.addAll(layer.modules());
    for (var parent : layer.parents()) {
      modules.addAll(getAllModules(parent));
    }
    return modules;
  }

  private record Property(String key, String value) {

    static List&lt;Property&gt; ofEnvironment() {
      return System.getenv().entrySet().stream()
          .map(e -&gt; {
            var key = e.getKey();
            var value = e.getValue();
            return new Property(key, fixValue(key, value));
          })
          .toList();
    }

    static List&lt;Property&gt; ofSystemProperties() {
      return System.getProperties().stringPropertyNames().stream()
          .map(key -&gt; {
            var value = System.getProperty(key);
            return new Property(key, fixValue(key, value));
          })
          .toList();
    }

    private static String fixValue(String key, String value) {
      if (value == null) return null;
      return value.transform(src -&gt; {
        var sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i &lt; src.length(); i++) {
          char c = src.charAt(i);
          var s =
              switch (c) {
                case '\f' -&gt; &quot;\\f&quot;;
                case '\t' -&gt; &quot;\\t&quot;;
                case '\r' -&gt; &quot;\\r&quot;;
                case '\n' -&gt; &quot;\\n&quot;;
                default -&gt; Character.toString(c);
              };
          sb.append(s);
        }

        var res = sb.toString();
        if (key.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT).contains(&quot;path&quot;) &amp;&amp; !key.equals(&quot;path.separator&quot;)) {
          res = res.replace(File.pathSeparatorChar, '\n');
        }
        return res;
      });
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>
<h4>Maven</h4>
<p>pom.xml:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;

&lt;project xmlns=&quot;http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0&quot;
         xmlns:xsi=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance&quot;
         xsi:schemaLocation=&quot;http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd&quot;&gt;
  &lt;modelVersion&gt;4.0.0&lt;/modelVersion&gt;

  &lt;groupId&gt;com.example&lt;/groupId&gt;
  &lt;artifactId&gt;jfxapp&lt;/artifactId&gt;
  &lt;version&gt;0.1.0-SNAPSHOT&lt;/version&gt;

  &lt;properties&gt;
    &lt;project.build.sourceEncoding&gt;UTF-8&lt;/project.build.sourceEncoding&gt;
    &lt;maven.compiler.release&gt;25&lt;/maven.compiler.release&gt;

    &lt;native-image.executable&gt;native-image&lt;/native-image.executable&gt;
  &lt;/properties&gt;

  &lt;build&gt;
    &lt;pluginManagement&gt;
      &lt;plugins&gt;
        &lt;plugin&gt;
          &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.maven.plugins&lt;/groupId&gt;
          &lt;artifactId&gt;maven-toolchains-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
          &lt;version&gt;3.3.0&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/plugin&gt;
        &lt;plugin&gt;
          &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.maven.plugins&lt;/groupId&gt;
          &lt;artifactId&gt;maven-antrun-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
          &lt;version&gt;3.2.0&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/plugin&gt;
        &lt;plugin&gt;
          &lt;groupId&gt;org.codehaus.mojo&lt;/groupId&gt;
          &lt;artifactId&gt;exec-maven-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
          &lt;version&gt;3.6.3&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/plugin&gt;
        &lt;plugin&gt;
          &lt;groupId&gt;org.graalvm.buildtools&lt;/groupId&gt;
          &lt;artifactId&gt;native-maven-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
          &lt;version&gt;1.1.11&lt;/version&gt;
        &lt;/plugin&gt;
      &lt;/plugins&gt;
    &lt;/pluginManagement&gt;

    &lt;plugins&gt;
      &lt;plugin&gt;
        &lt;groupId&gt;org.codehaus.mojo&lt;/groupId&gt;
        &lt;artifactId&gt;exec-maven-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
        &lt;executions&gt;
          &lt;!-- Execution to run the Java code directly --&gt;
          &lt;execution&gt;
            &lt;id&gt;java-run&lt;/id&gt;
            &lt;configuration&gt;
              &lt;executable&gt;java&lt;/executable&gt;
              &lt;arguments&gt;
                &lt;arg&gt;--module-path&lt;/arg&gt;
                &lt;modulepath/&gt;
                &lt;arg&gt;--enable-native-access&lt;/arg&gt;
                &lt;arg&gt;javafx.graphics&lt;/arg&gt;
                &lt;arg&gt;--module&lt;/arg&gt;
                &lt;arg&gt;jfxapp/com.example.jfxapp.Main&lt;/arg&gt;
              &lt;/arguments&gt;
            &lt;/configuration&gt;
          &lt;/execution&gt;

          &lt;!-- Execution to run the native image --&gt;
          &lt;execution&gt;
            &lt;id&gt;native-run&lt;/id&gt;
            &lt;configuration&gt;
              &lt;executable&gt;${project.build.directory}/bin/jfxapp&lt;/executable&gt;
            &lt;/configuration&gt;
          &lt;/execution&gt;
        &lt;/executions&gt;
      &lt;/plugin&gt;
    &lt;/plugins&gt;
  &lt;/build&gt;

  &lt;profiles&gt;

    &lt;!-- Profile that adds '.cmd' to the 'native-image' executable --&gt;

    &lt;profile&gt;
      &lt;id&gt;win&lt;/id&gt;
      &lt;activation&gt;
        &lt;os&gt;
          &lt;family&gt;windows&lt;/family&gt;
        &lt;/os&gt;
      &lt;/activation&gt;
      &lt;properties&gt;
        &lt;native-image.executable&gt;native-image.cmd&lt;/native-image.executable&gt;
      &lt;/properties&gt;
    &lt;/profile&gt;

    &lt;!-- Profile that uses 'exec-maven-plugin` to build the native image --&gt;

    &lt;profile&gt;
      &lt;id&gt;exec&lt;/id&gt;
      &lt;build&gt;
        &lt;plugins&gt;
          &lt;plugin&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.maven.plugins&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;maven-antrun-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;executions&gt;
              &lt;execution&gt;
                &lt;!-- 
                  Invoking 'native-image' via the 'exec-maven-plugin' will not 
                  automatically create the 'bin' directory, so we do that here.
                --&gt;
                &lt;id&gt;make-bin-dir&lt;/id&gt;
                &lt;phase&gt;initialize&lt;/phase&gt;
                &lt;goals&gt;
                  &lt;goal&gt;run&lt;/goal&gt;
                &lt;/goals&gt;
                &lt;configuration&gt;
                  &lt;target&gt;
                    &lt;mkdir dir=&quot;${project.build.directory}/bin&quot;/&gt;
                  &lt;/target&gt;
                &lt;/configuration&gt;
              &lt;/execution&gt;
            &lt;/executions&gt;
          &lt;/plugin&gt;

          &lt;plugin&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.codehaus.mojo&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;exec-maven-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;executions&gt;
              &lt;execution&gt;
                &lt;id&gt;native-compile&lt;/id&gt;
                &lt;phase&gt;package&lt;/phase&gt;
                &lt;goals&gt;
                  &lt;goal&gt;exec&lt;/goal&gt;
                &lt;/goals&gt;
                &lt;configuration&gt;
                  &lt;executable&gt;${java.home}/bin/${native-image.executable}&lt;/executable&gt;
                  &lt;arguments&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;--module-path&lt;/arg&gt;
                    &lt;modulepath/&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;--enable-native-access=javafx.graphics&lt;/arg&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;-Ob&lt;/arg&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;-o&lt;/arg&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;${project.build.directory}/bin/jfxapp&lt;/arg&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;--module&lt;/arg&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;jfxapp/com.example.jfxapp.Main&lt;/arg&gt;
                  &lt;/arguments&gt;
                &lt;/configuration&gt;
              &lt;/execution&gt;
            &lt;/executions&gt;
          &lt;/plugin&gt;
        &lt;/plugins&gt;
      &lt;/build&gt;
    &lt;/profile&gt;

    &lt;!-- Profile that uses 'native-maven-plugin' to build the native image --&gt;

    &lt;profile&gt;
      &lt;id&gt;buildtools&lt;/id&gt;
      &lt;build&gt;
        &lt;plugins&gt;
          &lt;plugin&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.graalvm.buildtools&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;native-maven-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;executions&gt;
              &lt;execution&gt;
                &lt;id&gt;native-compile&lt;/id&gt;
                &lt;phase&gt;package&lt;/phase&gt;
                &lt;goals&gt;
                  &lt;goal&gt;compile-no-fork&lt;/goal&gt;
                &lt;/goals&gt;
                &lt;configuration&gt;
                  &lt;quickBuild&gt;true&lt;/quickBuild&gt;
                  &lt;outputDirectory&gt;${project.build.directory}/bin&lt;/outputDirectory&gt;
                  &lt;imageName&gt;jfxapp&lt;/imageName&gt;
                  &lt;mainClass&gt;com.example.jfxapp.Main&lt;/mainClass&gt;
                  &lt;buildArgs&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;--add-modules&lt;/arg&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;javafx.controls&lt;/arg&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;--enable-native-access&lt;/arg&gt;
                    &lt;arg&gt;javafx.graphics&lt;/arg&gt;
                  &lt;/buildArgs&gt;
                &lt;/configuration&gt;
              &lt;/execution&gt;
            &lt;/executions&gt;
          &lt;/plugin&gt;
        &lt;/plugins&gt;
      &lt;/build&gt;
    &lt;/profile&gt;

    &lt;!-- Profile that enables toolchain support --&gt;

    &lt;profile&gt;
      &lt;id&gt;toolchain&lt;/id&gt;
      &lt;build&gt;
        &lt;plugins&gt;
          &lt;plugin&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.maven.plugins&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;maven-toolchains-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;executions&gt;
              &lt;execution&gt;
                &lt;id&gt;default-cli&lt;/id&gt;
                &lt;phase&gt;validate&lt;/phase&gt;
                &lt;goals&gt;
                  &lt;goal&gt;toolchain&lt;/goal&gt;
                &lt;/goals&gt;
                &lt;configuration&gt;
                  &lt;toolchains&gt;
                    &lt;jdk&gt;
                      &lt;version&gt;[25,)&lt;/version&gt;
                      &lt;vendor&gt;BellSoft&lt;/vendor&gt;
                      &lt;!-- 
                        The 'nik' is to distinguish between &quot;normal&quot; and NIK distributions. The
                        'full' is to distinguish between &quot;standard&quot; (no JavaFX) and &quot;full&quot; (with
                        JavaFX) distributions.

                        Edit or remove this, or edit your 'toolchains.xml', as needed so the
                        toolchains match.
                      --&gt;
                      &lt;variant&gt;nik-full&lt;/variant&gt;
                    &lt;/jdk&gt;
                  &lt;/toolchains&gt;
                &lt;/configuration&gt;
              &lt;/execution&gt;
            &lt;/executions&gt;
          &lt;/plugin&gt;

          &lt;plugin&gt;
            &lt;groupId&gt;org.codehaus.mojo&lt;/groupId&gt;
            &lt;artifactId&gt;exec-maven-plugin&lt;/artifactId&gt;
            &lt;executions&gt;
              &lt;execution&gt;
                &lt;id&gt;native-compile&lt;/id&gt;
                &lt;configuration&gt;
                  &lt;!-- 
                    When using a toolchain we only want to specify the executable name, not the
                    full path. That way the 'exec-maven-plugin` looks in the toolchain for the
                    executable.
                  --&gt;
                  &lt;executable&gt;${native-image.executable}&lt;/executable&gt;
                &lt;/configuration&gt;
              &lt;/execution&gt;
            &lt;/executions&gt;
          &lt;/plugin&gt;
        &lt;/plugins&gt;
      &lt;/build&gt;
    &lt;/profile&gt;

  &lt;/profiles&gt;
&lt;/project&gt;
</code></pre>
<h3>Build &amp; Execute</h3>
<p>Here are the different ways to build and execute the example. For every command, you can
activate the <code>toolchain</code> profile to make use of toolchains if the <em>BellSoft Liberica Full NIK</em>
installation is not <code>JAVA_HOME</code>. Multiple profiles can be activated by passing a comma-separated
list of profile IDs.</p>
<h4>Compile and run as a normal Java application</h4>
<p>This command compiles the code and runs it via <code>java</code>. It does not create a native image.</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>mvn clean process-classes exec:exec@java-run
</code></pre>
<h4>Compile native image with <code>exec-maven-plugin</code> and run it</h4>
<p>This command compiles the code, creates a native image via the <code>exec-maven-plugin</code> plugin, then
runs the native image.</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>mvn clean package exec:exec@native-run -P exec
</code></pre>
<h4>Compile native image with <code>native-maven-plugin</code> and run it</h4>
<p>This command compiles the code, creates a native image via the <code>native-image-plugin</code> plugin, then
runs the native image.</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>mvn clean package exec:exec@native-run -P buildtools
</code></pre>
<p>Remember that <code>JAVA_HOME</code> or <code>GRAALVM_HOME</code> need to be set to the Liberica NIK location in this
case.</p>
<h3>Building &amp; Executing from IDE</h3>
<p>How you execute the above Maven commands from your IDE depends on the IDE you're using. The three
major Java IDEs (IntelliJ IDEA, Eclipse, NetBeans) should all provide a way to execute Maven
commands. Code editors like VS Code likely also provide a way.</p>
<p>Consult your IDE's / code editor's documentation for more information.</p>
<hr />
<h1>Some Notes</h1>
<ul>
<li><p>According to its Q&amp;A, Liberica NIK does not fully support JavaFX's media and web functionality.</p>
<blockquote>
<h3>02. Does GraalVM and NIK support JavaFX?</h3>
<p>Yes, but only if you choose to utilize the NIK-full build of Liberica Native Image Kit. The
media and web functions of JavaFX are not fully implemented. That means that native images
created with Liberica JDK will run JavaFX-based applications in case they don’t utilize media
and web functionality.</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li><p>The native image created on Windows will open a terminal window when launched. This is quite
inconvenient for a GUI application, but I don't know the solution.</p>
</li>
<li><p>The native images built by <code>exec-maven-plugin</code> and <code>native-maven-plugin</code> above are not exactly
the same. The biggest difference is the former builds a native image for a modular application,
whereas the latter does not. I don't know how to get <code>native-maven-plugin</code> to define the
<code>--module</code> argument, if it's possible.</p>
</li>
</ul>

Q: Using jQuery, how can I scroll to a particular div on a page is centered (vertical and horizontal)? A: <p><strong>Working Example:</strong> <a href="http://jsfiddle.net/wonq8es4/3/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">http://jsfiddle.net/wonq8es4/3/</a></p>

