Q: How to create a 3d array by creating a subarray for each grouping record with CodeIgniter A: <p>drop the <code>group by OD.product_id</code> from the query first, it throws away the rows you need. Then group in php while you iterate:</p>
<pre><code>$rows = $this-&gt;db-&gt;query($sql)-&gt;result_array();
$out = array();
foreach ($rows as $r) {
    $pid = $r['product_id'];
    if (!isset($out[$pid])) {
        $out[$pid] = array(
            'product_id'   =&gt; $pid,
            'product_name' =&gt; $r['product_name'],
            'order'        =&gt; array(),
        );
    }
    $out[$pid]['order'][] = array(
        'order_detail_id' =&gt; $r['order_detail_id'],
        'user_id'         =&gt; $r['user_id'],
        'order_id'        =&gt; $r['order_id'],
    );
}
$out = array_values($out);
</code></pre>
<p>keying by product_id is what makes the lookup cheap, and <code>array_values()</code> at the end gives you the 0,1,2 numbering your sample shows. works on ci2 / php 5.3 as written.</p>
